{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal diffusivity from material properties thermal diffusivity from material properties","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","fileName":"Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermophysical Material Characterization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermophysical Material Characterization","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal diffusivity from material properties thermal diffusivity from material properties","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","fileName":"Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties","heading":"Thermal Diffusivity from Material Properties","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Thermal diffusivity is the ratio of thermal conductivity to density times specific heat capacity, $\\alpha=k/(\\rho c_p)$. It characterizes how rapidly a temperature disturbance spreads through a material relative to the material's capacity to store energy.\n\nBecause it is derived from three other properties, a thermal model can compute it rather than require it as an independent input. Laser-flash analysis can measure its temperature dependence b